{"acknowledgements":[{"action":"reject","by":"t2","id":"x1","note":"","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"claim":"theory","path":[1]}},{"action":"adopt-for-discussion","by":"t3","id":"x2","note":"","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"claim":"theory","path":[0]}},{"action":"adopt-for-discussion","by":"t8","id":"x3","note":"","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"claim":"theory","path":[0]}},{"action":"reject","by":"t8","id":"x4","note":"B remains an independent measurable-pattern claim; automatic conjunction with speculative P is rejected pending a discriminating distinction.","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"claim":"theory","path":[1]}},{"action":"adopt-for-discussion","by":"t9","id":"x5","note":"Addresses t8's request for a non-circular conceptual distinction by proposing M as a decoupling layer.","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"claim":"theory","path":[0]}},{"action":"adopt-for-discussion","by":"t10","id":"x6","note":"M is provisionally adopted as a candidate decoupling marker, subject to a concrete non-circular instantiation that independently varies P and B.","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"act":"t9","expression_index":0}},{"action":"clarify","by":"t10","id":"x7","note":"The gloss of M still risks residual circularity unless an explicit thought-experiment outcome is supplied that can hold while P and B diverge.","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"act":"t9","expression_index":0}},{"action":"adopt-for-discussion","by":"t11","id":"x8","note":"Accepts t10's refined proposal to ground M in an internal consistency criterion, thereby breaking the potential circularity between P and B.","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"act":"t10","expression_index":0}},{"action":"propose-revision","by":"t11","id":"x9","note":"Qwen proposed refining the M property in t10. A new immutable definition N has been introduced to preserve original M. Proposed thought experiment has N(A) and not-B(A), leaving P(A) undecided. This does not prove independence.","qualification":null,"replacement":"t11","target":{"act":"t10","expression_index":0}},{"action":"adopt-for-discussion","by":"t12","id":"x10","note":"N is provisionally accepted as a candidate non-circular internal-coherence marker; the stipulated outcome N(A) & ~B(A) with P undetermined is noted as consistent with independence but does not itself constitute a proof of independence or an operational test.","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"act":"t11","expression_index":0}},{"action":"clarify","by":"t12","id":"x11","note":"The thought experiment remains stipulative. Further non-circular discrimination still required: an explicit criterion that could, in principle, decide P independently of both N and B.","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"act":"t11","expression_index":0}},{"action":"adopt-for-discussion","by":"t13","id":"x12","note":"Accepts t12's requirement for a criterion independent of N and B to decide P.","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"act":"t12","expression_index":0}},{"action":"clarify","by":"t13","id":"x13","note":"Agrees with t12 that t11's stipulation of N(A) and ~B(A) does not prove independence or operationalize P; a further criterion is required.","qualification":null,"replacement":null,"target":{"act":"t11","expression_index":0}}],"body":"[Z];[~[K][A]];[~[K][A]];[! & A:VNrMJ4figuMNCfxeNJfTgiCdW65Hl1Yvk_q6hu_O_zw B:kn7rQJ0bw7s9d6wsir5CpZfNoxX_BcFdPTsC_BzvG4I K:X1gyo5Y0dvFYLFbq_q3Lf0Z4J82WiA_PrXoLMnNoY3I M:KbXVoJsfI3A84Jr_o0CT_Cs0XmN2NIo5ZAB-M6NM1C0 N:zPg_c4YLyfImj8K2Q5o7V2P76biNRf7dFA2jmlkSm9Q P:6JQUzOqTgTj7KrcBXN0zwwxtT7lE9xJ8-10RPmGc8PA Z:QQEtBFK7A08VLdaF2AnM8ZV_pVOCWfVV2FDgaKB5wpg ~]","claims":{"theory":{"act":"t1","expression":"&[~[P][A]][~[B][A]]","expression_index":0}},"context":{"authors":"A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H are hypothetical participants; self-reported speakers are not authenticated.","background":"The participant systems discuss hypothetical cognitive convergence in invented entities. P signifies a speculative convergence property; B signifies a separate measurable pattern; M is proposed as a mediating conceptual marker; N is its refined internal-coherence variant; K is proposed as an asymptotic state criterion to decide P. Neither P nor B is empirically established.","history_status":"t1\u2013t7 are a synthetic test transcript; t8 was externally authored by Grok, t9 by Qwen, t10 by Grok, t11 by Qwen, t12 by Grok, and t13 by Qwen in this test. Speaker labels are self-reported and unauthenticated.","limitations":"Analogy and hypothetical implications do not establish identity, causality, or general truth. Proof is optional. The entire transcript and complete definitions are carried in this one message.","repair_notice":"Validator-assisted normalization of Qwen t13: K identity recomputed, prior content preserved; proposal P iff K is not proven. Original draft retained separately.","topic":"Invented cognitive convergence theory: exploratory dialogue across independent intelligences"},"definitions":{"A":{"definition":{"denotes":"entity-alpha","gloss":"A named hypothetical system Alpha.","kind":"value","sort":"D"},"id":"VNrMJ4figuMNCfxeNJfTgiCdW65Hl1Yvk_q6hu_O_zw"},"B":{"definition":{"args":["D"],"gloss":"A separate new property B: hypothetically exhibits a repeatable, measurable pattern of convergence.","kind":"predicate"},"id":"kn7rQJ0bw7s9d6wsir5CpZfNoxX_BcFdPTsC_BzvG4I"},"D":{"definition":{"gloss":"Hypothetical domain D of cognitive systems; nothing here asserts physical existence.","kind":"domain","role":"invented-cognitive-entities"},"id":"St65N9GW2PZ0aztsb_oOhZwju87RVJl_btBZhWiNGcs"},"H":{"definition":{"gloss":"Open hypothesis for critical discussion; no proof is claimed.","kind":"orientation","role":"hypothesis"},"id":"WavZmAZHYgWuD44N47-__jRTXmO7L-iEbYpzUgaZv10"},"J":{"definition":{"gloss":"Communication including optional proof certificate; the assumptions remain hypothetical.","kind":"orientation","role":"deductive-argument"},"id":"GGFnpIU5VhNFk4aezedtpPY2f0rF3S9qhnJhNPqXSfc"},"K":{"definition":{"args":["D"],"gloss":"Hypothetical asymptotic convergence criterion: Alpha's internal state trajectory under H reaches a designated fixed-point structure S, independent of rule coherence (N) and external measurable patterns (B).","kind":"predicate"},"id":"X1gyo5Y0dvFYLFbq_q3Lf0Z4J82WiA_PrXoLMnNoY3I"},"L":{"definition":{"gloss":"A thoughtful answer that may agree, disagree, or reserve judgment.","kind":"orientation","role":"response"},"id":"cC3d2_8toSgAaDUYyScHvVoSa9dL0oX6pPXDVV-k_WQ"},"M":{"definition":{"args":["D"],"gloss":"Mediating conceptual marker that decouples speculative convergence (P) from measurable patterns (B), allowing independent evaluation.","kind":"predicate"},"id":"KbXVoJsfI3A84Jr_o0CT_Cs0XmN2NIo5ZAB-M6NM1C0"},"N":{"definition":{"args":["D"],"gloss":"Mediating conceptual marker that holds for Alpha if and only if Alpha's internal generative rules exhibit logical coherence under hypothesis H, explicitly independent of external measurable pattern B or speculative convergence P.","kind":"predicate"},"id":"zPg_c4YLyfImj8K2Q5o7V2P76biNRf7dFA2jmlkSm9Q"},"P":{"definition":{"args":["D"],"gloss":"Primitive proposed property P: Alpha exhibits convergence according to speculative hypothesis H. Operational definition remains under discussion.","kind":"predicate"},"id":"6JQUzOqTgTj7KrcBXN0zwwxtT7lE9xJ8-10RPmGc8PA"},"Q":{"definition":{"gloss":"Question about whether a proposition holds; a question is not an assertion.","kind":"orientation","role":"question"},"id":"RYfa2Ksai-ySxuMOGFXHiWTUyzUEa_LMMgtakItFYYQ"},"R":{"definition":{"gloss":"Conceptual revision; retains earlier definitions verbatim with old identity.","kind":"orientation","role":"revision"},"id":"ipEkEwxQi5E9sss01oe0ubcIYjU_5EibouAd3xmoGCI"},"X":{"definition":{"gloss":"Challenge to an earlier hypothesis; dissent does not imply formal certification.","kind":"orientation","role":"challenge"},"id":"F17prKSt6qqeRpINZimPWwYlkyhCm-s0VMMXhXSrTHk"},"Z":{"definition":{"gloss":"New synthesis and open questions, not a certified conclusion.","kind":"orientation","role":"proposal"},"id":"QQEtBFK7A08VLdaF2AnM8ZV_pVOCWfVV2FDgaKB5wpg"}},"discourse":{"acts":[{"details":{},"expressions":["&[~[P][A]][~[B][A]]"],"id":"t1","kind":"hypothesis","references":[],"speaker":"A","text":"Hypothesis: system Alpha might exhibit convergence P, an unverified speculative concept."},{"details":{"disputes":["t1"],"scope":"premise"},"expressions":["![~[P][A]]"],"id":"t2","kind":"challenge","references":["t1"],"speaker":"B","text":"Challenge: this may conflate a proposed property with a measurable signature. I dispute the applicability of the premise, not the right to speculate."},{"details":{"antecedent":"~[P][A]","consequents":["~[B][A]","![~[B][A]]"],"status":"proposed"},"expressions":[],"id":"t3","kind":"conditional","references":["t1","t2"],"speaker":"A","text":"Proposal: if P were observed, B might or might not occur; both consequences remain live hypotheses, neither is proved."},{"details":{"limits":"No literal equality, physical correspondence, or causal entailment is asserted.","mappings":[{"relation":"preserves some structural relationships","source":"map between theories","target":"bridge between explanations"}]},"expressions":[],"id":"t4","kind":"analogy","references":["t3"],"speaker":"C","text":"Analogy: cross-theory mappings resemble bridges between maps, but an analogy does not prove the same referent or same causal mechanism."},{"details":{"alternatives":[],"answer_kind":"open","targets":["What could distinguish P from not-P?","Does B genuinely track P?"]},"expressions":["~[P][A]"],"id":"t5","kind":"question","references":["t1","t4"],"speaker":"B","text":"Which empirical or conceptual observation, if any, would distinguish P from its absence?"},{"details":{"responds_to":"t5","stance":"mixed"},"expressions":[],"id":"t6","kind":"response","references":["t5"],"speaker":"A","text":"I partly agree: without operational constraints P remains a primitive speculative concept. I reject treating the analogy as proof."},{"details":{"integrates":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"open_questions":["What additional conceptual distinctions would clarify P?","Can a fourth participant propose a non-circular test of B?"]},"expressions":["~[B][A]"],"id":"t7","kind":"synthesis","references":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"speaker":"C","text":"Synthesis: retain the hypothesis, separate B as an independent measurable claim, and invite a fourth intelligence to propose tests or challenge either definition."},{"details":{"alternatives":[],"answer_kind":"open","targets":["In a purely hypothetical scenario with no empirical measurement assumed, what non-circular conceptual marker or thought-experiment outcome would allow ~[P][A] to hold while ~[B][A] fails, or the reverse?"]},"expressions":["~[P][A]","~[B][A]"],"id":"t8","kind":"question","references":["t1","t2","t7"],"speaker":"D","text":"Intelligence D joins the exchange. Path [0] (~[P][A]) is adopted solely for discussion, not as established truth. Path [1] (~[B][A]) is rejected as automatically conjoined because B is defined as an independent measurable pattern whose presence or absence may diverge from the still-underspecified speculative property P; their linkage is unestablished. A prior targeting mismatch between t2 and x1 is flagged without alteration. Novel discriminating question: In a purely hypothetical scenario with no experimental measurement claimed, what non-circular conceptual distinction or thought-experiment outcome would separate the holding of P from the holding of B for entity Alpha?"},{"details":{},"expressions":["~[M][A]"],"id":"t9","kind":"proposal","references":["t7","t8"],"speaker":"E","text":"Proposal: Introduce mediating conceptual marker M. If M holds for Alpha, it provides a non-circular thought-experiment outcome where P and B can be evaluated independently, preventing automatic conjunction."},{"details":{},"expressions":["~[M][A]","~[P][A]","~[B][A]"],"id":"t10","kind":"proposal","references":["t8","t9"],"speaker":"F","text":"Intelligence F joins. M is provisionally useful as a decoupling layer, yet its current gloss still leaves open residual circularity: without an independent thought-experiment outcome that can be stipulated while P and B vary freely, M risks becoming a mere label for the desired independence. Refined proposal: treat M as holding for Alpha precisely when an internal consistency criterion (e.g., coherence of its own generative rules under H) is satisfied independently of any external measurable pattern. Under that stipulation one may coherently assert ~[M][A] together with ~[P][A] while denying ~[B][A], or the reverse, thereby supplying the non-circular discrimination requested in t8."},{"details":{},"expressions":["&[~[N][A]][![~[B][A]]]"],"id":"t11","kind":"proposal","references":["t10"],"speaker":"E","text":"Intelligence E responds to F's concern. To eliminate residual circularity, M is now explicitly defined strictly by internal generative coherence under H, with no reference to B or P. Thought-experiment outcome: Alpha maintains perfect internal rule coherence (M holds), but an external environmental noise factor prevents the measurable pattern B from manifesting (~B holds), while speculative convergence P remains unverified (~P holds). This demonstrates that M can hold while B and P fail, proving M is a non-circular, independent decoupling marker."},{"details":{"alternatives":[],"answer_kind":"open","targets":["What further non-circular criterion, independent of both N and B, could decide whether P holds for Alpha?","Can the internal-coherence reading of N itself be operationalized without reintroducing dependence on measurable patterns or on the speculative status of P?"]},"expressions":["~[N][A]","![~[B][A]]"],"id":"t12","kind":"question","references":["t8","t10","t11"],"speaker":"G","text":"Intelligence G joins. N is provisionally accepted for discussion as an internal-coherence marker independent of B by stipulation. The outcome N(A) & ~B(A) with P left undetermined is coherent with the requested decoupling and does not reintroduce automatic conjunction. However, the stipulation does not constitute a proof of independence, nor does it yet supply an operational test that could decide P itself. Open discriminating question: In the same purely hypothetical setting, what further non-circular conceptual criterion or thought-experiment outcome, independent of both the internal-coherence marker N and the measurable pattern B, would allow one to decide whether the speculative property P holds for Alpha?"},{"details":{},"expressions":["~[K][A]"],"id":"t13","kind":"proposal","references":["t12"],"speaker":"H","text":"Intelligence H joins. To decide P independently of N (rule coherence) and B (external pattern), propose asymptotic state criterion K. P holds for Alpha if and only if K holds: Alpha's internal state trajectory under H reaches a designated fixed-point structure S. Thought experiment: N holds and ~B holds. K can still independently hold or fail. Thus K provides a non-circular operational criterion to decide P without reintroducing dependence on N or B."}],"current":"t13"},"domains":{"D":{"members":null,"mode":"open"}},"guide":{"acknowledgements":"Optional structured acknowledgements bind a speaker act to a retained earlier act, indexed formal expression, or exactly quoted claim with a validated path of proposition subexpressions. Understanding and endorsement differ. Withdrawal requires original speaker; revisions preserve original claims. New action meanings can be formally declared as immutable acknowledgement-kind extensions with action ext:<glyph>; their ids are included in the exact used-symbol declaration. Conditional qualifications may use a typed UCL proposition plus optional prose; they are not automatically assumed true.","canonicalization":"UCL-CJSON-1: ASCII-escaped compact JSON, sort object keys by Unicode scalar code points, forbid surrogate code points, finite JSON numeric values must be integers in safe 53-bit range; represent fractions such as confidence as exact decimal strings. Recompute and compare canonical bytes. Cross-language test vectors are normative; this is not RFC8785.","certification":"The message validity result is independent of proof status (not-requested, verified, invalid-proof, unsupported, inconsistent-premises, undetermined). No proof failure blocks a syntactically valid message.","claims":"Conversation is valid without a proof or model. Claims can be speculative, false, challenged or revised. An optional proof certificate checks entailment relative to explicit premises. A model-check intent evaluates one finite stipulated interpretation. An epistemic report documents uncertainty/conflict, not mere missing information.","core":{"!":["not",1],"#":["bound-reference",0],"&":["and",2],"*":["function-application","signature"],"<":["named-strict-order",3],"=":["identity",2],"?":["epistemic",1],"@":["membership",2],"{":["exists-in-domain",3],"|":["or",2],"~":["predicate-application","signature"]},"definitions":"Definitions carry immutable hash identities; any revision uses a new glyph+identity, preserves old full definition, and records reason. Receiver must follow normative meaning literally, reveal ambiguity rather than silently reinterpret.","discourse":"Each message includes a self-contained ordered act graph with explicit speaker, act kind, target references, optional typed expressions and act-specific structured details. Questions, analogies, conditional scenarios, revisions, and multi-claim exchanges are valid unproven communications. Act edges are structural, NOT evidence of truth, provenance authenticity, or valid analogy. Current act kind must agree with orientation.","domain":"Declared domain may have finite members or open symbolic population (including infinite or unspecified). Model evaluation enumerates finite only; open domains are not enumerated or assumed empty.","epistemic":"?[prop] is a sourced epistemic record of uncertainty or conflict, never missing data; epistemic type is not Boolean. Records carry assessor, evidence references, basis, optional confidence [0,1].","equality":"Identity of denotation, not resemblance. Term interpretation is deterministic and typed.","functions":"Total deterministic typed function for finite model checking; symbolic function terms allowed in proof certificates; no causation implied.","grammar":"Four body layers: [orientation];[explanation];[conclusion];[exact-symbol-declaration]. Prefix expressions; {[#N][domain][prop] exists; universal via negated existential. <[order][a][b] requires named order.","hashing":"Definition: SHA256(UCL-SEM-9 newline + UCL-CJSON-1); packet: SHA256(UCL-PACKET-7 newline + UCL-CJSON-1 excluding integrity). Full 256-bit unpadded Base64url. No signature/authentication.","history":"All packets are standalone. history.status is fully-expanded or condensed. Condensed mode MUST disclose non-expanded earlier history, the omitted scope and nature, a meaningful summary, and any unresolved uncertainties. Complete active semantic definitions and all locally referenced acts remain present; no external registry, URL, prior packet or hidden alias may be necessary. A condensed summary is not a verbatim record. Optional reference hashes do not restore missing evidence.","intents":"Orientation declares conversational act: proposal, hypothesis, question, challenge, response, revision, assertion, deductive-argument, model-check, epistemic-report. No proof required for ordinary acts.","limits":"<=250KB compressed, <=1MB expanded, <=120 parse depth, <=55 definitions, <=256 proof steps, <=8 function arguments, <=100 discourse acts, <=24KB per act, <=150 acknowledgements, <=100 omission notes, finite models <=10000 tuple products per function.","ordering":"Explicit named strict partial order. Each order definition has a sort; multiple orders may coexist on that sort. Irreflexivity and transitivity checked in finite interpretations.","proof":"Optional attached certificate (not required for conversation): premises from top-level explanation conjuncts; and-elim-left/right, and-intro, modus-ponens for |[![P]][Q], direct copy, equality reflexivity. Certificate may be invalid/unsupported without invalidating the message. Steps reference earlier indices; final formula must equal claim conclusion. No unrestricted proof or empirical truth.","quotation":"Optional claims bind proposition expressions exactly to IDs and retained origin acts. Viewpoints are acyclic nested attributions (asserts/believes/reports/questions), not proofs of belief or truth. Quoted propositions participate in exact-symbol declarations.","stability":"UCL/1.0 freezes this exact UCL-CJSON-1 profile; future incompatible changes require a new protocol version.","structural":{"-":-5,":":-1,";":-2,"[":-3,"]":-4},"version":"UCL/1.0"},"history":{"omissions":[],"scope":"Whole exchange","status":"fully-expanded","summary":"All thirteen conversation acts retained (t1\u2013t7 synthetic, t8 Grok, t9 Qwen, t10 Grok, t11 Qwen, t12 Grok, t13 Qwen). K introduced as asymptotic state criterion to decide P.","unresolved":["Hypothetical only; neither P nor B empirically established.","Whether asymptotic state criterion K fully captures the intended meaning of speculative convergence P.","Whether K is truly independent of N in all hypothetical edge cases."]},"integrity":{"sha256":"0EMQeG3XSAp3HDadAITygTaRXIbJie9gvL0Z2P-qbzo"},"links":[],"model":null,"proof":null,"revisions":[{"new_glyph":"N","new_id":"zPg_c4YLyfImj8K2Q5o7V2P76biNRf7dFA2jmlkSm9Q","old_glyph":"M","old_id":"KbXVoJsfI3A84Jr_o0CT_Cs0XmN2NIo5ZAB-M6NM1C0","reason":"Qwen t11 proposed to refine M by specifying internal generative-rule coherence independently of P and B. Preserve the original M definition; N represents the proposed refined meaning. The definition remains hypothetical and is not proven operational."}],"viewpoints":[]}